  "notes": "Yanbu Cement Company (ticker 3060, a Saudi Joint Stock Company) audited consolidated financial statements for the year ended 31 December 2025 with FY2024 comparatives, from the full audited PDF in the 'Annual / 2025' cell of the Saudi Exchange company-profile 'Financial Statements' tab (Resources/fsPdf/428_0_2026-03-11...). Auditor: BDO Dr. Mohamed Al-Amri & Co. (Maher Al-Khatieb, registration 514); unqualified opinion, dated Jeddah 11 March 2026. The consolidated financial statements were approved by the Board of Directors on 14 Ramadan 1447H (corresponding to 3 March 2026) - Note 41. Amounts are presented in full Saudi Riyals (scale 1) except per-share data. The primary statements (printed FS pages 4-8) are scanned images in the filed PDF (transcribed from page renders at 2.7x); the notes are digital text. Consolidated group; there is **NO non-controlling interest** (net profit and equity are not split), so only total_equity is carried. There are no discontinued operations - the standard pre-tax - zakat bridge applies. **FY2024 comparatives are RESTATED / reclassified (Note 40)** - certain items (including intangible assets and related cash-flow lines) were reclassified retrospectively with no impact on the statement of changes in equity; the figures carried here are the restated comparatives as presented on the face statements. investments_associates / share_of_profit_associates are 'Investment in an associate' / 'Share of net loss from an associate' (a loss both years); other_noncurrent_assets is 'Other non-current assets' (nil FY2025, so only the FY2024 fact is carried); other_current_assets is the 'Financial derivative' current-asset line; short_term_investments is 'Investments at fair value through profit or loss (FVTPL)'; cash is the 'Bank balances' line. other_reserves is the 'Statutory reserve'. long_term_debt is the non-current 'Bank borrowings'; current_debt combines 'Current portion of bank borrowings' and 'Short term financing'; provisions is 'Provision for site restoration' (quarry); defined_benefit_obligation is 'Provision for employees' defined benefits obligations'; other_current_liabilities is 'Dividends payable'; accrued_expenses is 'Accrued expenses and other current liabilities'; zakat_payable is 'Zakat payable'. On the P&L: operating_income is 'PROFIT FROM OPERATIONS'; other_income is 'Other income, net'; other_nonoperating_expense is 'Loss on derivative instruments at fair value through profit or loss'; other_nonoperating_income is 'Gain on investments at fair value through profit or loss (FVTPL)'; finance_income and finance_costs are the reported 'Finance income' / 'Finance cost'; income_taxes_and_zakat is the 'Zakat' charge. On the cash-flow statement: depreciation_amortization combines PP&E depreciation and intangible-asset amortisation; interest_paid is 'Finance cost paid'; zakat_paid is 'Zakat paid'; capex combines 'Purchase of property, plant and equipment' and 'Purchase of intangible assets'; debt_issued is 'Proceeds from short-term financing'; debt_repaid combines 'Payment of bank borrowings' and 'Payment of short-term financing'; lease_payments is 'Payment of lease liability' (nil FY2025, only the FY2024 fact carried); dividends_paid is 'Dividends paid'; the cash-flow statement has no FX-on-cash line and its 'BANK BALANCES AT THE END OF THE YEAR' equals the balance-sheet 'Bank balances' line exactly. FY2025 was a weaker year - a jump in selling and distribution expenses and cost of revenue took operating profit down from SAR 179.7m to SAR 128.4m and net profit from SAR 157.1m to SAR 104.5m (EPS 0.66). Statement page references are the printed FS page numbers: profit or loss 4, comprehensive income 5, financial position 6, changes in equity 7, cash flows 8.",
